course: dictionary
lesson: 4196
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the clues around them show which one the writer means. «Sophie put googly eyes on everything in the fridge, and when Mum opened it a dozen eyes stared at her.» Googly eyes are big, round toy eyes that stick on things, so here they are silly plastic eyes, not real ones.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. Here it is about crafts, stuck-on eyes and a surprised Mum, so googly means the wobbly, bulging kind. A word can also change its job: googly can describe eyes, or it can name a cricket ball.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «a dozen googly eyes stared at her» make sense? Yes, so the first meaning fits the story.
fact: Googly is an informal word. «Googly eyes» are big, round eyes that stick out, often toy plastic eyes with a loose black dot that wobbles.
fact: In «Sophie put googly eyes on everything in the fridge», the eyes are stuck onto objects, which makes them look silly.
fact: In cricket, a googly is a tricky ball bowled by a spin bowler. It turns the opposite way from what the batter expects.
fact: Cricket is played in the UK, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland, and the googly is a famous trick ball for fooling the batter.
fact: The same word can mean different things, so look at the clues in the sentence to find the right meaning.
exercise: What are googly eyes in «Sophie put googly eyes on everything in the fridge»? | Real eyes that can see very well | Eyes that are always shut | *Big round toy eyes that stick out and wobble
exercise: In cricket, what is a googly? | *A tricky ball that turns the opposite way from what the batter expects | A cake sold at the village fair | A big glove worn by the wicket keeper
exercise: «Mum laughed and the photo went on the family group chat.» Find and copy the word that tells you how many eyes there were in the fridge. | *dozen | photo | family | fridge
test: In cricket, a googly is bowled by which kind of bowler? | A fast bowler | A goalkeeper | A batter | *A spin bowler
test: In «googly eyes», what does googly mean? | *Big, round and sticking out | Very quiet | Long and thin | Able to see in the dark
exam: Which clue shows that googly means the eyes in «Sophie put googly eyes on everything in the fridge»? | The photo was sent to the group chat | Googly is the name of Sophie | *Eyes stuck on things, in a sentence about crafts and the fridge | The word is about bowling and batters
